    "final_answer": "I have successfully found the information for the word \"resilience\" in the Cambridge Dictionary. Here are the details:\n\n## Word: \"resilience\"\n\n### Pronunciation\n- **UK (British):** /rɪˈzɪl.jəns/\n- **US (American):** /rɪˈzɪl.jəns/\n- **Formal variant:** resiliency — UK /rɪˈzɪl.jən.si/, US /rɪˈzɪl.jən.si/\n\n**Part of speech:** noun [C2]\n\n### Definitions\n\n**Definition 1:** The ability to be happy, successful, etc. again after something difficult or bad has happened.\n\n**Definition 2:** The ability of a substance to return to its usual shape after being bent, stretched, or pressed.\n\n### Sample Sentences\n\n**For Definition 1:**\n- *\"Trauma researchers emphasize the resilience of the human psyche.\"*\n- *\"These are habits that can break down the resiliency you'll need to help you through difficult times.\"*\n\n**For Definition 2:**\n- *\"The plant fibre has incredible strength and resilience.\"*\n- *\"These new materials have additional resiliency and elasticity properties, as well as great strength.\"*\n\n**Source:** Cambridge Advanced Learner's Dictionary & Thesaurus (© Cambridge University Press)",
